= The Militant Tendency

Labour's National Executive has voted to set up a register of the groups that work inside the party, aimed at the Militant Tendency, a Trotskyist organisation with its own newspaper, its own full-time organisers and, its critics say, its own membership. Militant is strong in the Liverpool Labour Party, and its supporters have been selected to fight a few safe Labour seats. The leadership backs the register; the left says a witch-hunt has begun.

- @militant_campaign: Make Militant the face of Labour.
- @stay_out: Leave Labour to its quarrel.

@militant_campaign
subtitle: -1 resource. Labour's moderates suffer along with the rest.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; labour_credibility -= 4; c2_lab -= 1; de_lab -= 0.5; labour_civil_war += 5; wet_dissent += 1

Central Office prints the names of the Militant candidates, quotes from their newspaper and a simple question: is this the party you want to govern Britain?

@stay_out
on-arrival: labour_civil_war += 2

You say nothing. Labour's quarrel needs no help from you, and it gets none.

